WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.930
- Each year at Commencement,

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:11.020
our university recognizes
an exceptional group

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:13.803
of individuals with Honorary Degrees.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.630
These degrees are the most
significant distinction

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:20.100
conferred by the Yale Corporation,

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.470
the university's Board of Trustees,

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:25.780
to signal pioneering
achievement in a field

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:29.020
or conspicuous and exemplary contribution

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:30.163
to the common good.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:32.640
Though we cannot adorn

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.030
this year's Honorary Degree recipients

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:36.723
in their academic hoods,

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:41.120
or applaud their
accomplishments as they stand

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.653
on the Commencement stage,

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:47.160
we gather from our computers, phones,

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:51.240
and devices around the
world to recognize the ways

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.190
in which they have expanded our knowledge

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:56.820
and gifted us with their art,

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:00.113
song, scholarship, and innovation.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.060
Today, we honor nine individuals
who serve as examples

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:08.700
to our graduates and members
of the Yale community.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.820
They encourage us to aspire to excellence

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:15.310
and to value those
elements of human character

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:17.430
that they embody;

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:22.430
creativity, curiosity,
discipline, integrity,

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.563
and a passion for public service.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:29.630
Their association with the Class of 2020

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:32.453
also honors the students
who graduate today.

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:37.210
Collectively they represent
the aspirations of Yale

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:38.453
as an institution.

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:42.740
It is now my distinct pleasure

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:46.630
to announce the 2020
honorary degree recipients

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:48.030
and to confer their degrees.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.980
For the degree of Doctor of Laws,

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:56.423
Jerome Alan Cohen, Legal Scholar.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:00.450
Pioneering scholar of Chinese law,

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:03.480
you have taught and
mentored countless others

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:06.743
in a field you helped
establish in this country.

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:08.860
A courageous voice

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:12.160
for those whose voices have been silenced,

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:15.093
you defend human rights around the globe.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:19.280
Bold trail blazer and advocate,

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:24.190
for using your many talents
to create a more just world,

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:28.450
we are proud to present you
with your third Yale degree,

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:30.603
Doctor of Laws.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.370
For the degree of Doctor of Music,

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:39.943
Herbie Hancock, Musician and Composer.

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:43.270
Chameleon of modern jazz,

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:45.820
you have shown us new possibilities

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:48.993
and encouraged us to
imagine a better world.

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:53.270
By experimenting with science and sound,

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:56.250
you let your talent take you, and us,

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:58.080
to new places,

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:00.650
breaking down barriers between genres

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:04.983
and creating chords of
peace that connect humanity.

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:08.900
Wonderful wizard and musical icon,

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:11.810
Yale is delighted to confer on you this

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:13.993
Doctor of Music degree.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:21.000
For the degree of Doctor
of Humane Letters,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.343
Christiana Figueres, Public Servant.

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:29.220
Your diplomacy has brought
people and nations together

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:31.450
to address one of the
most important issues

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:33.793
of our time, climate change.

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:37.470
Building bridges instead of borders,

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:39.593
you've led countries to action,

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:44.280
helping forge international
accords to ensure the health

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:48.253
and survival of future
generations on this planet.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.530
Global citizen, skilled leader,

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:53.530
Yale is honored

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:56.963
to award you this Doctor
of Humane Letters degree.

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:03.110
For the degree of Doctor of
Engineering and Technology,

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:07.163
Michael I. Jordan, Computer Scientist.

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:11.470
Facing an uncertain and complex world,

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:15.240
you harness the power of
human and machine learning

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:17.920
to solve daunting problems.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:21.490
By bridging disciplines and
following your curiosity,

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:25.493
you have made possible what
was once only imagined.

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:31.430
Explorer of new domains,
champion of big ideas,

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:34.260
in recognition of the
doors you have opened

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:36.480
and the networks you have built,

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:41.480
we proudly bestow on you
this Doctor of Engineering

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:44.223
and Technology degree.

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:49.390
For the degree of Doctor of Fine Arts,

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:53.003
Ming Cho Lee, Theatrical Set Designer.

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:56.760
You have set the world on stage

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:59.673
and your influence circles the globe.

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:03.320
Your classroom is legendary.

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:05.340
With insight and humility,

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:09.260
you inspired thousands of Yale
students to create new vistas

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:11.363
of art and meaning.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:16.110
Generous teacher, visionary artist,

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:19.590
for helping us see, feel, and
understand the great drama

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:21.780
of human life anew,

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:24.340
we are delighted to confer on you

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:27.083
this Doctor of Fine Arts degree.

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:31.400
For the degree Doctor of Science,

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:35.763
Svante Pääbo, Evolutionary Geneticist.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:40.330
From bone fragments
thousands of years old,

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:42.730
you show us what has endured

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:45.940
and what has been lost from ancient times

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:47.113
to the present day.

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:52.220
Applying the latest science
to age old questions,

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:55.940
you have revealed secrets
about the prehistoric world,

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:58.840
discovered previously unknown species,

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:01.763
and invented a new field of study.

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:04.790
Passionate scientist,

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:09.720
for opening a window onto
our ancestors and ourselves,

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:12.820
Yale is privileged to confer on you

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:15.453
this Doctor of Science degree.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:20.060
For the degree of Doctor of Music,

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:22.393
Renée Fleming, Soprano.

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:25.860
You have shared your extraordinary voice

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:28.120
on the world's greatest stages,

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:32.730
thrilling audiences with
you repertoire and range.

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:35.140
Transcending styles and traditions,

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:38.550
you champion the importance
of music for our health,

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:40.663
minds, and communities.

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:46.690
Soaring soprano, lyrical
ambassador of the arts,

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:51.710
for helping us hear all the
octaves of life more clearly,

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:54.080
we are honored to present you

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:56.923
with this Doctor of Music degree.

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:02.580
For the degree of Doctor
of Medical Sciences,

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:06.003
Jim Allison, Immunologist.

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:09.630
Your discoveries have
transformed the science

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:11.250
of cancer treatment,

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:14.540
opening up new frontiers in medicine.

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:17.360
By unleashing the power of T-cells,

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:19.940
you enlisted the body's own immune system

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:22.530
to combat this terrible disease,

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:26.923
and your research has restored
health and hope to patients.

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:31.010
Laureate and lifeline,

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:35.470
in honor of the futures
you have made possible,

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:37.650
we gratefully bestow on you

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:41.143
this Doctor of Medical Sciences degree.

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:47.080
And for the degree of Doctor of Letters,

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:50.053
Paula Vogel, Playwright and Educator.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:55.620
While waltzing or
driving, dying or loving,

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:58.500
your characters connect with audiences

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:01.563
and bring urgent issues
out of the shadows.

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:03.880
A devoted teacher,

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:06.090
you foster the future of theater,

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:09.030
helping young playwrights
find their voices

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:11.320
and refine their craft.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:13.550
In appreciation for your brave artistry

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:15.600
and spirited mentorship,

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:20.600
Yale is proud to award you
this Doctor of Letters degree.

00:08:22.570 --> 00:08:26.143
I send my warm
congratulations to all of you.

00:08:27.010 --> 00:08:28.990
The entire university joins me

00:08:28.990 --> 00:08:31.620
in applauding your accomplishments.

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:34.663
Welcome, to the Class of 2020.

